{
  "_comment": [
    "pt-BR grocery lexicon. Read by lib/core/staples.dart; every field also has a",
    "compile-time default in Staples.fallback, so a missing file is not a crash.",
    "",
    "staples: what a term is SOLD as at a Paraná supermarket.",
    "  \"kg\"  — loose, priced per kilo (hortifruti, açougue, frios no balcão)",
    "  \"un\"  — a package, priced per package (mercearia, bebidas, limpeza)",
    "  Shorthand: a bare string is the sale unit. The object form adds",
    "  \"sizes\" (retail package sizes) and \"packs\" (how many come in one).",
    "",
    "This distinction is the whole point: it decides whether the 5 in",
    "\"Arroz 5kg\" is five kilos to buy (amount) or the size of one bag (size).",
    "Guessing that from syntax alone is impossible — hence this file."
  ],
